Identify the geographical location of the Great Lakes and the Atlantic Ocean to determine their meeting point.
Based on the provided context, the Great Lakes are located primarily in the upper mid-east region of North America, on the Canada–United States border, which connects to the Atlantic Ocean through the Saint Lawrence River. 

The Atlantic Ocean is located to the east of Europe, Africa, and the Strait of Gibraltar, and it merges into the Indian Ocean in the southeast. 

Therefore, the meeting point of the Great Lakes and the Atlantic Ocean is at the Saint Lawrence River, which is located on the Canada–United States border.
