What is the historical context of the Public Service Commission (PSC) in India, specifically its establishment and role in the civil service system, and how does it relate to the Union Public Service Commission (UPSC)?
The Public Service Commission (PSC) in India was established as a constitutional authority to oversee appointments, transfers, promotions, and disciplinary matters related to the civil service. It was later reconstituted as the Federal Public Service Commission. The Union Public Service Commission (UPSC) is the premier central recruiting agency in India, responsible for appointments to and examinations for All India services and group A & group B of Central services. The UPSC's charter is granted by Part XIV of the Constitution of India, and it is mandated by the Constitution for appointments to the services of the Union and All India Services.
