Describe the structure and function of the pulmonary artery, including its origin and destination.
The pulmonary artery is a major blood vessel in the heart and lungs. It originates from the right ventricle of the heart and has two main branches: the left pulmonary artery and the right pulmonary artery. 

The left pulmonary artery descends through the left side of the thorax and passes through the aortic arch to reach the left lung. The right pulmonary artery descends through the right side of the thorax and passes through the right main bronchus to reach the right lung.

The pulmonary arteries carry deoxygenated blood from the heart to the lungs, where it picks up oxygen and releases carbon dioxide through the process of gas exchange. The oxygen-rich blood then returns to the heart through the pulmonary veins and is pumped out to the rest of the body.
