What is the definition of a hat-trick in a Test match, and how is it achieved by a bowler in both innings?
A hat-trick in cricket occurs when a bowler dismisses three batsmen with consecutive deliveries. In a Test match, a bowler achieves a hat-trick by taking three wickets in three consecutive deliveries, which can be in the same over or across multiple overs, as long as they are consecutive deliveries by the individual bowler in the same match.
