What is the current composition and leadership structure of the Rajya Sabha?
The Rajya Sabha, also known as the Council of States, is a house of the Parliament of India. It is a bicameral legislature with two houses: the Rajya Sabha and the Lok Sabha. The Rajya Sabha has 245 members, with 233 members elected by the elected members of the state legislative assemblies through a single transferable vote system and 12 members nominated by the President of India. 

The leadership structure of the Rajya Sabha includes the Chairman, who is the presiding officer of the House, and the Deputy Chairman. The Chairman is elected by the members of the House from among themselves. The Leader of the House is the leader of the majority party or coalition in the House, and the Leader of the Opposition is the leader of the largest opposition party. 

As of my last update in 2021, the composition and leadership structure of the Rajya Sabha may have changed due to the dynamic nature of politics and elections. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking the official website of the Rajya Sabha or other reliable news sources.
