What is the historical context and purpose of the Great Pyramid of Giza, and who was likely to be buried within it based on ancient Egyptian burial practices and pharaonic succession?
Based on the provided context, the Great Pyramid of Giza was built as a tomb for the Fourth Dynasty Egyptian pharaoh Khufu (also known as Cheops) over a 10- to 20-year period. In ancient Egyptian burial practices, the pyramid served not only as a tomb for the pharaoh but also as a storage pit for items the pharaoh would need in the afterlife. Given the pharaonic succession, it is likely that Khufu's son or successor would have been buried in a separate pyramid, following the tradition of building a pyramid for each pharaoh.
