When was the Uniform Time Act of 1966 passed, and what were its key provisions regarding daylight saving time?
The Uniform Time Act of 1966 was passed on April 13, 1966. Its key provisions regarding daylight saving time (DST) were:

*   DST began nationwide on the last Sunday in April
*   DST ended on the last Sunday in October
*   Clocks would be advanced one hour beginning at 2:00 a.m. on the last Sunday in April
*   Clocks would be turned back one hour at 2:00 a.m. on the last Sunday in October
*   States were allowed to exempt themselves from DST as long as the entire state did so.
