What was the specific date or period when the Cherokee Nation was forcibly relocated from their ancestral lands to the west, and what were the circumstances surrounding this event?
The Cherokee Nation was forcibly relocated from their ancestral lands to the west between 1836 and 1839. This event, known as the Trail of Tears, was a result of the forced relocation of the Cherokee Nation from their lands in Georgia, South Carolina, North Carolina, Tennessee, Texas, and Alabama to the Indian Territory (present-day Oklahoma) in the then Western United States. The relocation resulted in the deaths of an estimated 4000 Cherokee.
