What is the background and context of the song 'Eye of the Tiger', including its release date and notable associations?
The song "Eye of the Tiger" was made famous by the rock band Survivor. According to the band, the song's title was initially considered too obvious, and they had considered calling it "Survival" instead. The song's lyrics were written with a rhyme scheme that included the word "rival" to rhyme with "survival", but they ultimately decided to go with "Eye of the Tiger". The song became a hit and is often associated with the 1982 film Rocky III, in which it was featured. It has since become a classic rock anthem and a cultural icon.
